ears from 1951 to 2025, and July to August came in under 90% of normal in 35 of them, more than any other pair on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids. In 2025, August to September came in at 46% of normal on that middle. So far in 2026, January to February sits at 46% and May to June at 133%. On grid 23577 a preliminary estimate puts August to September 2026 at 171.4, and RMA&rsquo;s final index can differ.</p>"}
